WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.212
A marsh can look like wasted land.

2
00:00:02.212 --> 00:00:03.791
It is actually doing three jobs at

3
00:00:03.791 --> 00:00:04.683
once.

4
00:00:05.083 --> 00:00:07.312
First, it cleans water.

5
00:00:07.312 --> 00:00:09.402
Plants slow the flow,

6
00:00:09.402 --> 00:00:10.772
mud settles out,

7
00:00:10.772 --> 00:00:12.281
and the water that moves on is

8
00:00:12.281 --> 00:00:13.314
cleaner.

9
00:00:13.314 --> 00:00:15.683
That is why wetlands are called nature's

10
00:00:15.683 --> 00:00:16.807
kidneys.

11
00:00:17.207 --> 00:00:19.494
Second, it works like a sponge.

12
00:00:19.494 --> 00:00:21.503
It soaks up floodwater and releases it

13
00:00:21.503 --> 00:00:24.556
slowly, which lowers floods downstream and keeps

14
00:00:24.556 --> 00:00:26.656
streams flowing in the dry season.

15
00:00:27.056 --> 00:00:28.380
In the United States,

16
00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:31.654
wetlands along the Mississippi once stored at

17
00:00:31.654 --> 00:00:33.997
least sixty days of floodwater.

18
00:00:34.397 --> 00:00:36.522
Third, it is home.

19
00:00:36.522 --> 00:00:37.659
Fish breed in it,

20
00:00:37.659 --> 00:00:39.482
and birds like these painted storks at

21
00:00:39.482 --> 00:00:41.663
Keoladeo in Rajasthan come to feed.

22
00:00:42.063 --> 00:00:45.279
Keoladeo and Chilika lake in Odisha were

23
00:00:45.279 --> 00:00:47.462
India's first two Ramsar sites,

24
00:00:47.462 --> 00:00:49.133
in nineteen eighty-one.

25
00:00:49.133 --> 00:00:50.991
The Ramsar treaty itself was signed in

26
00:00:50.991 --> 00:00:52.998
Iran in nineteen seventy-one.

27
00:00:53.398 --> 00:00:55.708
For Prelims: wetlands filter water,

28
00:00:55.708 --> 00:00:57.496
store floods and shelter life.

29
00:00:57.496 --> 00:00:58.843
The treaty is Ramsar,

30
00:00:58.843 --> 00:01:00.339
nineteen seventy-one.

